'''Malastare Narrows''' was a location on the [[planet]] [[Malastare]]<ref name="BMF 64" /> in the [[Mid Rim Territories]].<ref name="Malastare">{{Databank|malastare|Malastare}}</ref> In [[34 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> prior to the [[First Battle of Geonosis|outbreak]] of the [[Clone Wars]]<ref name="Trench Enc">{{SWE|characters|admiraltrench|Admiral Trench}}</ref> between the [[Galactic Republic]] and [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]],<ref name="Cat and Mouse" /> a [[Corporate Alliance]]<ref name="HC 78">{{HelmetCollectionCite|78|Databank A-Z}}</ref> [[Corporate fleet (Malastare)|fleet]] [[Commanding officer|commanded]] by the [[Harch]] [[Admiral]] [[Trench]] had formed a [[blockade]] around Malastare.<ref name="Cat and Mouse" />

The Republic then [[Battle of Malastare Narrows|dispatched]] a [[fleet]] of [[starship]]s to break Trench's blockade and destroy his fleet,<ref name="Cat and Mouse" /> but were pushed back several [[time]]s with significant losses sustained.<ref name="HC 78" /> Afterward, the matters were resolved when a [[Kep-She's task force|task force]]<ref name="Cat and Mouse" /> led by [[Jedi Master]] [[Kep-She]]<ref name="Ep Guide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode216.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Cat and Mouse}}</ref> destroyed [[Trench's flagship]]. The outcome led to presumptions of the Harch's [[death]], including by [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]]. However, Trench was discovered to have survived the battle, as he led a Separatist [[Christophsis blockade|blockade]] at the [[Battle of Christophsis]] during the Clone Wars<ref name="Cat and Mouse" /> in [[22 BBY]].<ref name="Timelines" />

==Behind the scenes==
Malastare Narrows was first mentioned in "[[Cat and Mouse]],"<ref name="Cat and Mouse" /> the sixteenth episode of the [[The Clone Wars: Season One|second season]] of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' television series, which aired on [[March 26]], [[2010]].<ref name="Ep Guide" />

